From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: the prompt template in a saved image's parameters

img_gen and vid_gen take two more optional body fields, "template" and
"negative_template": the text the prompt was made from (the web UI's {a|b}
and __name__ placeholders), as strings of at most 8000 bytes (another type or
a longer text is a 400, as other bad fields are). A saved image or video then
has them in its parameters, as A1111's Dynamic Prompts writes them:
"Template: <t>, Negative Template: <n>, " in front of "Preset:" (a value with
a comma, a colon, a quote or a line break is a JSON string, like A1111's
quote()), and "template" and "negative_template" in the "ps5sd" object of
sd.cpp's JSON. "template" is written when it is not empty; "negative_template"
whenever the body had it, an empty one as "", so a reader can tell an empty
negative prompt from no template information. The request carries them as
ImgGenJobRequest::prompt_template and VidGenJobRequest::prompt_template to
save_output_images and save_output_video; without the fields the output is
the same as before.
